  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "KEROV’S CENTRAL LIMIT THEOREM FOR SCHUR-WEYL MEASURES OF PARAMETER α = 1/2 — In this article, we show that Kerov’s central limit theorem related to the ﬂuctuations of Young diagrams under the\n\n**KEROV’S CENTRAL LIMIT THEOREM FOR SCHUR-WEYL MEASURES OF PARAMETER α = 1/2**\n\n*PIERRE-LOÏC MÉLIOT*\n\n23 pp, 8 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** In this article, we show that Kerov’s central limit theorem related to the ﬂuctuations of Young diagrams under the Plancherel measure extends to the case of Schur-Weyl measures, which are the probability measures on partitions associated to the representations of the symmetric groups Sn on tensor products of vector spaces V ⊗n (see [Bia01]). The proof is inspired by the one given in [IO02] for the Plancherel measure, and it relies on the combinatorics of the algebra of observables of diagrams; we shall also use Śniady’s theory of cumulants of observables (cf. [Ś06]).\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Schur-Weyl measures of parameter =1/2; 2 Observables of diagrams; 3 Some computations around the limit shapes c; 4 Gaussian concentration of measures on partit; 5 Moments of the deviations and Chebyshev poly; 6 An extension of Kerov's central limit theore; References",
      "lang": "en",
